% Vasil Stoin, Narodna pesnopoyka (1930).
% Published early from the workshop on 11 November 2026: each tune names what is guessed or left out in its N: lines,
% and its workshop record (or review item) is kept for further correction.

X:1
T:Zdravets
T:Geranium (Здравец)
C:traditional (Bulgaria)
O:Bulgaria
R:horo song
S:Vasil Stoin, Narodna pesnopoyka (Sofia, 1930), No. 102 "Zdravets", p. 98
N:A Bulgarian horo song, sung while dancing the horo, the line dance of village festivities: two groups of singers, one at each end of the line, answer each other line by line. A question and its answer: "Little geranium, little wreath, do the girls pick you?" and the geranium tells how the girls pick it on St George's Day (6 May), weave it into wreaths and crown the lambs. Zdravets carries the word for health (zdrave) and is given for health at feasts. Count 9/16 as 2+2+2+3, quick-quick-quick-slow ("1 2 3 4-a"), and step a simple horo to it. Guessed: the second note of bar 3 in each line (read c; it could be B). Words in modern Bulgarian spelling (Stoin prints the pre-1945 spelling); transliteration and translation below are ours. Stoin marks it "fast"; the tempo, the tapan pattern and the held drone are ours.
Q:3/16=130
M:9/16
L:1/16
K:APhr
