w: здрав-че, вен-че, бе-рат ли те мо _ ми? _
w: Ка-то цъф-тя, все го-ра ми-ри _ ше. _
w: те си дой-дат ху-ба-ви де-вой _ ки, _
w: та ме но-сят на бър-зи по-то _ ци, _
w: и ме ту-рят на вак-ли а-гън _ ца. _
W:Transliterated (two lines to each time through the tune):
W:Zdravche, venche, berat li te momi? / Zdravche, venche, berat li te momi?
W:Ta mene li momi da ne berat? / Kato tsaftya, vse gora mirishe.
W:Kato doyde na den na Gergyovden, / te si doydat hubavi devoyki,
W:ta me berat vav novi tsedila, / ta me nosyat na barzi pototsi,
W:ta me viyat na zeleni ventsi / i me turyat na vakli agantsa.
W:
W:In English: "Little geranium, little wreath, do the girls pick you?" "How could the girls not pick me? When I bloom the whole forest smells sweet. When St George's Day comes, the pretty girls come; they pick me into new cloths, carry me to swift streams, weave me into green wreaths and put me on the dark-eyed lambs."
